# FloodPilot configuration
#
# Every variable here is optional. With none of them set, the app runs on live
# open data (Open-Meteo + OpenStreetMap) with an in-memory store — which is the
# point: it should work from a clean clone.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have.

# ── India Meteorological Department ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The authoritative source for rainfall over Delhi. With a key set, IMD becomes
# the primary rainfall provider and Open-Meteo becomes the fallback.
# Register at https://api.imd.gov.in/
# IMD_API_KEY=
# IMD_API_BASE=https://api.imd.gov.in

# ── Central Water Commission ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Yamuna gauge readings. https://cwc.gov.in/
# CWC_API_KEY=
# CWC_API_BASE=https://api.cwc.gov.in

# No API access yet? CWC publishes gauge readings as bulletins during flood
# events. A control room operator can enter the current reading directly.
# Danger level at Old Railway Bridge is 205.33 m.
# YAMUNA_LEVEL_M=204.10
# YAMUNA_TREND_M_24H=0.35

# ── Google Maps Platform ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Road elevation and live congestion derived from real travel times. Routing is
# never delegated to Google — it is used as a source, not as the decision-maker.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Switch from the in-memory store to PostGIS. Also run `npm install pg` and
# apply db/schema.sql. Without this, citizen reports live for the lifetime of a
# server instance.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/floodpilot

# ── Operations dashboard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Access code for /gov. Defaults to "delhi-flood-control" in development.
# A real deployment should put SSO in front of this route instead.
# GOV_ACCESS_CODE=

# ── Waterlogging register ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Civic bodies republish their waterlogging-point lists every monsoon, so the
# register is overridable without a deploy. Either a URL returning JSON, or
# inline JSON. Entries with a matching id replace the seeded ones; the rest are
# appended.
# FLOODPILOT_HOTSPOTS_URL=https://example.gov.in/waterlogging-points.json
# FLOODPILOT_HOTSPOTS_JSON=[]

# ── OpenStreetMap ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override the Overpass endpoint used by `npm run enrich:osm`.
# OVERPASS_API_URL=https://overpass.kumi.systems/api/interpreter
